<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Module 6 Worksheet</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1e293b;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 40px auto;
    max-width: 800px;
    padding: 0 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 26px;
    color: #0f172a;
    border-bottom: 3px solid #7b4fce;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  h2, h3 {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #7b4fce;
    margin-top: 35px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-left: 4px solid #00c8ff;
    padding-left: 12px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: #334155;
  }
  ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    padding-left: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  li {
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .checkbox {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-family: monospace;
    color: #94a3b8;
    margin-right: 10px;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .instructions {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #475569;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .question {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .response-box {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px dashed #7b4fce;
    border-left: 4px solid #7b4fce;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    margin: 10px 0 25px 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #475569;
  }
  .response-label {
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #7b4fce;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  .response-placeholder {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #94a3b8;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>PlayIQ Module 6 Worksheet: Retrieval and Correction</h1>
<div class="instructions"><strong>Instructions:</strong> Complete this worksheet thoughtfully. Remember, PlayIQ is about using AI as a coach, not a crutch. Your goal is to become an independent learner!</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 1: Why Rereading Fails</h3>
<div class="question">1. (Short Response) Why does rereading your textbook often trick you into thinking you are ready for a test?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">2. (Multiple Choice) What is "retrieval practice"?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Reading a paragraph three times.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Highlighting the most important words in a text.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Pulling the answer from your brain without looking at the notes.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Asking AI for the summary.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">3. (Prompt Improvement) You want to study a science chapter. Instead of rereading it, you decide to use AI. Write a prompt asking the AI to create a quick retrieval practice test, making sure it does *not* give you the answers right away.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">4. (Teach-Back) Explain to a friend why taking a blank piece of paper and trying to write out what you remember is a stronger study method than reading a chapter three times.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3>Part 2: Retrieval Practice System</h3>
<div class="question">5. (Short Response) A good self-test is not just random questions. What are the different *types* of questions a good retrieval test should include?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">6. (Classification) An AI asks you: "What year did the Civil War end?" Is this an easy recall question, an understanding question, or an application question?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">7. (Classification) An AI asks you: "If you were a general in the Civil War, how would you use the telegraph to win a battle?" Is this an easy recall question, an understanding question, or an application question?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">8. (Scenario) You took a 6-question retrieval test. You got both "easy recall" questions right, but missed the "application" question. What does this tell you about how you need to study next?</div>
