<h3>Part 3: Mistake Bank Patterns</h3>
<div class="question">9. (Short Response) Why is it helpful to treat a mistake as "data" instead of feeling bad about it?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">10. (Multiple Choice) You missed a math question because you wrote 5 x 4 = 15 instead of 20. What type of mistake is this?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Knowledge Gap</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Word Gap</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Careless Error</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Confidence Error</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">11. (Classification) You missed a science question because you didn't know what the word "mitosis" meant. Is this a Step Error, a Word Gap, or a Careless Error?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">12. (Scenario) You log three mistakes into your Mistake Bank. You notice a pattern: they are all "Step Errors" (you forget the middle step of long division). How does knowing this pattern help you study better?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">13. (Teach-Back) Teach someone else how classifying mistakes (like "Step Error" or "Word Gap") makes studying less frustrating.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
