<hr>
<h3>Part 4: Progressive Correction</h3>
<div class="question">14. (Short Response) What does "Progressive Correction" mean? Why isn't it enough to just look at the right answer once and move on?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">15. (Multiple Choice) When you review the mistakes from your Mistake Bank, what should the AI do?</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Give you the exact same questions so you can get a 100%.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Give you questions similar to the ones you missed, but change the examples or numbers.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Move on to a completely new topic.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Give you the final answers so you can memorize them.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">16. (Prompt Improvement) You want to review a mistake you made on a fractions quiz yesterday. Write a prompt asking the AI to re-test you, but asking it to change the numbers so you can't just memorize the answer.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">17. (Scenario) You get the new, changed question wrong again. Are you failing, or is the system working? Explain your answer.</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
